the end is finally here and the fate of  hawkins has never been more perilous  with max in a coma the gates to the  upside down completely open and the  mystery surrounding the soviet's role in  all of it it's time to explain what went  down during the ending of season 4 of  stranger things  what started as a series of riffs  opening beneath the town expands to  include the familiar snow-like particles  of the upside down drifting into the  real world while the rifts begin to  bellow smoke and red lightning crackles  in the clouds over the city our heroes  know very well what this means even if  no one else in town does something  bigger is coming to hawkins and soon the  question that remains as the season ends  though is what exactly that bigger  something will look like we've become  very familiar with the various kinds of  creatures who exist in the upside down  over the years so is vecna simply going  to stage an all-out assault with as many  of those beasts as he can summon is he  going to bring the mind player to  colossal life over the hawkins skyline  this is what our heroes have to figure  out as they head into season 5.  mike and eleven began season four with  serious issues in their relationship for  mike a big part of the problem was not  just the physical distance from elle who  moved to california with the buyer's  family but a perceived distance in their  personalities for him elle is an  exceptional person and he's simply not  and he's sure that one day she'll  realize that and decides she doesn't  need him 4l who's been struggling with  the loss of her powers at the end of  season 3 the problem is that she  believes mike doesn't feel as strongly  about her as she feels about him she  thinks her outsider status has made her  into a kind of monster that she can  never rehabilitate by the end of the  season they both learn they're wrong  will helps convince mike that he's vital  to their entire friend group and  eleven's life as the heart of the party  and the person who keeps everyone buoyed  by hope see how you're leading us here  you're guiding the whole party inspiring  us that's what you do  through her work with dr brenner eleven  comes to realize that she's not a  monster and that she's simply been  manipulated into perceiving some kind of  wrongness in her mind and body that  leads to an emotional reunion and  reconciliation at the end of the season  but the happiness is short-lived will  they get a happy ending or are they  destined to be ripped apart again  the hawkins kid faced an unimaginable  force of darkness as season 4  transitions into season 5 but that  doesn't mean their personal lives are  completely lost in the shuffle that's  perhaps clearest in the story of robin  who reveals a crush on a fellow student  named vicki at the beginning of the  season then sees things come a bit full  circle by the end in episode 8 robin  learns that vicki has a boyfriend from  out of town but one episode later when  she finds herself volunteering beside  her crush at hawkins high school she  learns that they broke up robin and the  newly single vicki are left to bond in a  real way making sandwiches for refugees  of the earthquake and laughing and  joking together right now it's hard to  imagine what anyone's life will look  like at the end of this fight but robin  seems closer than ever to the kind of  happy ending she deserves  jonathan byers and his girlfriend nancy  wheeler are separated by geography for  much of the fourth season but there's  also something else in the way of their  relationship since moving to california  jonathan has developed doubts about his  ability to ever be enough for nancy  particularly since he won't be going to  the same college she's hoping to attend  meanwhile back in hawkins nancy is very  aware of how distant jonathan's been and  that awareness coincides with the  re-emergence of steve harrington in her  life as they battle vecna together nancy  realizes that steve has grown a lot  since they broke up it seems like a  reconciliation might be in the cards but  then jonathan returns to hawkins putting  whatever might have happened on pause we  don't know what that means for season 5  just yet but it's pretty clear that  something has to give in this love  triangle joyce byers and jim hopper  spend most of season 4 trying to get  back to each other this is triggered  when joyce receives a message from  hopper that reveals he's being held in a  soviet prison joyce finally finds her  way to the prison only to find that  hopper's life is in a fresh kind of  danger it's only at the very end of the  season as they're working to find a way  to get back to america that the two can  come together as a proper couple once  again the happy reunion doesn't hold out  for long hopper and joyce make it back  to the states and time to find that the  kids fight against the upside down has  gone very wrong hawkins is now engulfed  in a full-on disaster as rifts open up  across the town the big question as we  head into season 5 is just how hopper  and joyce will make it through this  fight intact they lost each other once  already now they have to fight to make  sure it doesn't happen again  all of the hawkins kids are going  through their own major struggles in  stranger things four but will byers is  going through one of the hardest rough  patches of his young life in part  because he's doing much of it struggling  alone it's been speculated ever since a  key moment in season 3 that will is gay  l is not stupid it's not my fault you  don't like girls  fans think that eventually he'll come  out to his friends and perhaps even  reveal that he's in love with his best  friend mike wheeler in season 4 we get  more than one moment in which will seems  to allude to his secret in one very  potent moment near the end of the season  it seems like he's almost going to say  it but he keeps silent out of concern  for the larger fight will's personal  narrative remains stalled but it's clear  that he's aching to tell someone  something about the secret he's keeping  then there's will's other inner turmoil  something that hasn't been addressed  directly since season two will still has  at least some connection to the upside  down thanks to his possession by the  mind player once wekna launches his  invasion will's been feeling it more and  more will he be able to hold himself  together in the fight to come or is he  destined for an inner battle that's just  as dangerous as the external one near  the end of stranger things four eleven  makes a devastating discovery about her  puff-puff dr martin brenner she realizes  as brenner pushes her to stay in his  secret lab and cultivate her powers even  further that the experiments she  remembers from hawkins lab were never  about her they were always about using  her to get closer to henry he was  brenner's first patient who 11 cent to  the upside down in that hellish place he  transformed into the creature the kids  call vecta sometimes  papa doesn't tell the truth  it's a major moment of catharsis for 11  who realizes that the problem was never  her and her powers but it's also an  interesting wrinkle in the ongoing saga  of what was going on at hawkins lab it's  clear in season 4 that there are still  plenty of dark forces within the us  government who are squabbling over the  nature of the lab the upside down and 11  herself what's less clear is whether or  not anyone else knew about what brenner  was really trying to achieve if someone  did know are they out there trying to  finish his work does anyone else know  what henry has become these are the  questions that could have major  implications for what's coming in the  final season about halfway through  season four dr martin brenner and dr sam  owens form an uneasy alliance with the  shared goal of getting eleven's powers  back to full strength through the use of  the neenah machine by the end of the  season they're at odds again as owens  tries to let eleven leave to help her  friends and brenner is determined to  keep her in the lab longer to try and  reach one in the upside down then the  entire operation is disrupted when  lieutenant colonel sullivan and his  troops arrive killing brenner capturing  owens and trying to end the operation  once and for all by killing 11. by the  end of the season 11 is a fugitive from  the evil forces in the human world  pursuing her who wants her not just  contained but dead this explains why  she's going back into hiding in hopper's  cabin at the end of the season but what  we still don't know is just how far the  government will go to capture her  especially now that rifts have opened  all over hawkins it's a conflict that's  arguably just as important to her  survival as the fight against the upside  down  the end of stranger things 4 reveals  many things and not all of them come  from the united states during the  process of escaping from hopper's soviet  prison hopper and joyce discover a  secret lab full of preserved demogorgons  and demidogs as well as a chamber full  of swirling particles the soviets dubbed  the shadow this strange entity is later  revealed to be the dark material that  makes up the mind flare by the end of  the season the facility is basically  destroyed but its presence and brenner's  insistence that his experiments were all  about fighting the soviets raises some  interesting questions the soviet  government has its own operation tied to  the upside down perhaps geared towards  the weaponization of its creatures for a  fight against the west what remains to  be seen now is how that fight will  progress now that the prison facility is  destroyed  in an effort to defeat vekna before he  can invade hawkins max mayfield stages a  daring self-sacrificing trap for the  creature using her previous connection  to him to lure him out after some  coaxing the plan works but what doesn't  work quite as well were the parts of the  plan surrounding max's effort she's able  to lure vechna in and hide in a happy  memory for a while but the upside down's  pressure on her friends means that the  plot to kill vecta is delayed and max is  caught in the same psychic force that  killed three other hawkins teenagers by  the end of the battle vecna is driven  away but max is dead revived only by the  force of eleven's powers at the end of  the season max is in a coma in a  hospital bed her limbs broke and her  sight apparently gone and worse her  consciousness seemingly unreachable  eleven tries to go into her mind and  find her to search for some sign that  max is still in there somewhere and  isn't able to locate her so where is max  it's a big potentially devastating  question for season 5.  the final two episodes of stranger  things 4 reveal several new elements of  the show's backstory including how  vechna began to shape the upside down to  his will  i want you to tell her  everything you see  revealed through the discussion of his  backstory that once he was sent to the  upside down by eleven's powers he  wandered the landscape until he found  the shadow from there he sculpted it  into the mind flair making him the real  power behind the entire invasion of  hawkins even with that reveal there's a  good deal we still don't know about the  upside down it seems that many of the  dimensions creatures including  demigorgons were already inhabitants  when vechna got there now they're all  part of an extended hive mind of which  he is the master with the shadow  retaining a sort of symbiotic connection  to his will so what is the shadow why  does it work for vecna and what does  that mean for the larger fight there's  still so much we don't know about the  nature of this other dimension and that  feels like one of the biggest open  questions going into season 5.  at the end of part 1 of stranger things  4 nancy wheeler makes a shocking  discovery about the upside down or at  least about the version of hawkins that  exists within the upside down the entire  landscape is frozen in time a version of  hawkins as it existed in 1983 when  eleven first opened the gate in the lab  and released the first demogorgon it  seems that somehow at that moment a  duplicate version of hawkins emerged in  the upside-down landscape only to remain  frozen in time  we're in the past  at the moment it's not clear what that  means it's possible that 11's powers  accidentally created a weird mirror  image of hawkins lab and the surrounding  town at the moment she opened the gate  it could have something to do with  fekna's invasion plans whatever's going  on it's clear that the mirror image of  hawkins in the upside down will remain  an intriguing centerpiece of the  conflict going forward into season five  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  stranger things are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

